#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# sub_values

#% text
# `sub_values(f)` gives the rules defined for calls whose head is itself a call rooted at `f`, such as `f(x_)(y_) := ...`, as `lhs :> rhs` with the left side as it was written.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
rule adder(k_)(x_) := x + k

#% cell
sub_values(adder)
#% output
#= [adder(k_)(x_) :> x + k]

#% cell
adder(10)(5)
#% output
#= 15

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `down_values`, `up_values`, `own_values`
